      "side": 1,
      "message": "It doesn\u0027t sound like this analysis is correct. From the unlinkToDeath() documentation :\n\n```\n[returns] false if the target IBinder has already died, meaning the method has been (or soon will be) called.\n```\n\n```\nThrows NoSuchElementException if the given recipient has not been registered with the IBinder, and the IBinder is still alive. Note that if the recipient was never registered, but the IBinder has already died, then this exception will not be thrown, and you will receive a false return value instead.\n```\n\nIt doesn\u0027t look like this can happen if the binder has died ; instead it is explicitly documented to only happen when it has *not* died.\n\nAlso, this would imply the system server would crash with this every time the phone process crashes. I tested this, and it\u0027s not the case. I think what\u0027s happening is the phone process is crashing immediately as it unregisters the network provider. See inline for what I think is a better solution.",
